# Findings the image scan in CI may skip. Each entry needs a reason and an expiry date;
# after the date the scan fails on it again, so it has to be looked at once more.
# Trivy reads this file from the repository root.

# OpenSSL QUIC memory leak in Debian's libssl3t64, from the distroless base image. Debian had
# no fixed version on 2026-11-21. The app is not affected: Node carries its own OpenSSL
# (3.5.9) and never loads the system libssl3, which was checked by listing the libraries
# Node loads in the runtime image with https and tls in use. The app does not use QUIC.
# Remove this entry once a fixed base image is out and its digest is in the Dockerfile.
CVE-2026-124709 exp:2026-12-31

# OpenSSL QUIC denial of service (unbounded frame queueing) in the same Debian libssl3t64.
# Debian had no fixed version in any release on 2026-11-23. Same reasons as above: Node uses
# its own OpenSSL and never loads the system libssl3, and the app does not use QUIC.
# Remove this entry once a fixed base image is out and its digest is in the Dockerfile.
CVE-2026-107494 exp:2026-12-31
